---
import Layout from '../layout.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
const { profile } = site;
// A "now" page: who I am in two sentences, then what I'm up to lately.
// The convention comes from Derek Sivers (nownownow.com). Update the
// "What I'm doing now" section whenever life changes; the footer's
// Updated date is set automatically at build time.
---
<Layout title="Thadeus Smith – Now" description="Who Thadeus Smith is and what he is doing now.">
<article id="main">
<style>
/* Photo beside the opening paragraph; the image keeps the site's 6px border. */
.intro{
display: flex;
gap: 1rem;
align-items: flex-start;
margin: 0 0 1rem;
}
.intro img{
width: 8rem;
height: auto;
flex-shrink: 0;
}
.intro p{
margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
}
.credit{
font-size: 70%;
font-family: monospace;
font-weight: bold;
}
</style>
<h2>Now</h2>
<!-- Also marked up as an h-card; the note text lives in src/site.ts so this
     paragraph and the homepage's hidden h-card always match. -->
<div class="intro h-card">
<img class="u-photo" src={profile.photo} width={profile.photoWidth} height={profile.photoHeight} alt={profile.name}>
<div>
<p>Hello! My name (as the URL so helpfully indicates) is <span class="p-name">{profile.name}</span>. <span class="p-note">{profile.note}</span></p>
<p class="credit">Photo: <a href={profile.photoSource}>{profile.photoCredit}</a>, {profile.photoLicense}</p>
</div>
<data class="u-url" value={new URL('/', Astro.site).href}></data>
</div>

<h3>What I'm doing now</h3>
<p><b>Teaching.</b> I am the Director of Education at Lumos Debate, where I supervise our Boston-area classes, train our instructors, and run monthly tournaments. I am also a freelance speech & debate coach at national circuit competitions, primarily for the American Heritage School in Florida, and edit the Big Questions and Public Forum briefs for Champion Briefs.</p>
<p><b>Photographing.</b> I attended <a href="https://honkfest.org/">HONK!</a> and <a href="https://bostonbookfest.org/">Boston Book Festival</a> for <a href="https://wikiportraits.org/">WikiPortraits</a>. Turns out that my outdoor photography is a lot better than my indoor photography, but I bought some portrait-oriented lenses and am excited to try them out soon!</p>
<p><b>Editing.</b> I'm currently taking part in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Good_articles/GAN_Backlog_Drives/October_2026">October 2026 Good Article Nomination Backlog Drive</a>. Next month, I'll be participating in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:The_Asia-Oceania_Destubathon">Asia-Oceania Destubathon</a> and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Unreferenced_articles/Backlog_drives/November_2026">Unreferenced Articles November 2026 Backlog Drive</a>.</p>
<p><b>Reading.</b> I'm currently reading Michael Clune's <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/220687903-pan"><i>Pan</i></a>. Just finished Nicholas Binge's <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/61813107-ascension"><i>Ascension</i></a></p>
<p><b>Watching.</b> I'm currently watching <i>Slow Horses</i> and <i>Abbott Elementary</i> (both are great!), and I'm always drowning in my <a href="https://letterboxd.com/ThadeusOfNaz/watchlist/">Letterboxd watchlist backlog</a>.</p>

<p>This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about">now page</a>. If you have your own website, you should make one too.</p>
</article>
</Layout>
